   "sentenceId": 9,
   "he": "הַהֶקְדֵּשׁוֹת בִּשְׁלֹשָׁה. מַתְנִיתִין דְּלָא כִּי הַאי תַּנָּא, דְּתַנְיָא: רַבִּי אֱלִיעֶזֶר בֶּן יַעֲקֹב אוֹמֵר, אֲפִילּוּ צִינּוֹרָא שֶׁל הֶקְדֵּשׁ צְרִיכָה עֲשָׂרָה בְּנֵי אָדָם לִפְדּוֹתָהּ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that the valuation of «consecrated» property is performed «by three» judges. The Gemara comments: «The mishna is not in accordance with» the opinion of «this tanna, as it is taught» in a baraita: «Rabbi Eliezer ben Ya’akov says: Even» a simple item such as «a small fork of consecrated property requires» a valuation by «ten people» in order «to redeem it.»"
  }
